From 5c05f04ba041da3656561f053ea93b3c1ad6d1db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ci <ci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:56:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(outbound): preconnect keeps TCP conns to the proxy
 server warm

Add a `preconnect: N` option to every proxy. While the proxy carries
real traffic, its dialer keeps N connected TCP conns to the proxy
server, so a new connection skips the TCP handshake. It replaces the
anytls-only session preconnect.

The server address is the first one dialed over tcp by real traffic;
other addresses and packet dials pass through. The pool starts on the
first such dial and stops, closing its conns, after 15s without one.
Delay tests (URLTest) mark their context with C.WithHealthCheck and
neither start, extend nor take from it.

Pooled conns are recycled after 15s, or at 80% of the shortest idle
limit the server was seen to enforce. A 1ms read evicts conns the server
closed; bytes a server sends first, like an SSH banner, are kept and
handed back. Conns from a dialer-proxy are aged out only. TCP Fast Open
dials connect on their first write, so tfo turns preconnect off.
---
 adapter/adapter.go       |   3 +-
 adapter/outbound/base.go |   3 +-
 adapter/outbound/warm.go | 231 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 constant/healthcheck.go  |  16 +++
 4 files changed, 251 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 adapter/outbound/warm.go
 create mode 100644 constant/healthcheck.go

diff --git a/adapter/adapter.go b/adapter/adapter.go
index 422232b3..f2ac89bc 100644
--- a/adapter/adapter.go
+++ b/adapter/adapter.go
@@ -207,7 +207,8 @@ func (p *Proxy) URLTest(ctx context.Context, url string, expectedStatus utils.In
 	}
 
 	start := time.Now()
-	instance, err := p.DialContext(ctx, &addr)
+	// Marked so that a delay test does not keep preconnected conns warm.
+	instance, err := p.DialContext(C.WithHealthCheck(ctx), &addr)
 	if err != nil {
 		return
 	}
